# Trivy Ignore Policy
#
# This file intentionally contains no active suppressions by default.
# Findings must not be ignored globally or permanently without a documented
# risk-acceptance decision.
#
# Supported identifiers may include:
#   - CVE-...       Vulnerability findings
#   - GHSA-...      GitHub Security Advisory findings
#   - AVD-AWS-...   Terraform / IaC misconfiguration findings
#   - DS...         Secret scanning findings
#   - GPL-...       License findings, where supported by the configured scanner
#
# Rules for adding an exception:
# 1. Use the exact Trivy finding ID only.
# 2. Never ignore by package name, provider name, severity, or wildcard.
# 3. Add a by package name, provider name, severity, or wildcard.
# 3. Add a the finding over suppressing it.
# 5. Use a time-bounded exception and define an owner/review date.
# 6. Do not suppress HIGH or CRITICAL findings without explicit security approval.
# 7. Validate every exception against the actual scan target and file path.
#
# Example:
#
# CVE-YYYY-NNNN
# AVD-AWS-XXXX
#
# The examples above are intentionally disabled and must not be uncommented
# without a verified finding and an approved risk-acceptance record.
#
# Recommended review metadata for each exception:
#   ID: <finding-id>
#   Reason: <why remediation is temporarily not possible>
#   Owner: <plus-or-github-handle>
#   Tracking: <issue-or-risk-acceptance-reference>
#   Review-by: <YYYY-MM-DD>
#
# No active suppressions are approved at repository bootstrap.
